  <section class="tab-panel" id="protocol" role="tabpanel" data-tab-title="Protocol">
    <h2>How Rule-Loading Works</h2>

    <p>The protocol was built around a simple contract: <strong>discover, read, cite, respond</strong>. Before answering any user prompt, the model must execute a four-gate sequence encoded in <code>AGENTS.md</code>. Each gate produces a verifiable artifact&mdash;a tool call, a file read, a structured citation&mdash;that the eval harness can inspect post-hoc.</p>

    <p>The motivation is straightforward: a library of domain-specific rules (Snowflake SQL conventions, deployment checklists, security policies) is maintained independently of model training data. Models must consult the <em>current</em> version of these rules, not their parametric memory of what the rules <em>used to say</em>. The protocol enforces this by requiring a tool-call read of the actual file before the model may claim it as loaded.</p>

    <h3>The Four Gates</h3>

    <p><strong>Gate 1: Foundation.</strong> The model reads a single foundational rule file (<code>000-global-core.md</code>) that applies to every interaction. This is the baseline&mdash;if Gate 1 fails, nothing else proceeds.</p>
    <p><strong>Gate 2: Discovery.</strong> The model identifies which domain-specific rules are relevant to the current user prompt. It does this by extracting keywords from the prompt and searching a compact index file (<code>RULES_INDEX.md</code>). The protocol supports two paths: a primary path using a delegated skill, and a fallback path using direct grep.</p>
    <p><strong>Gate 3: Loading.</strong> For each rule identified in Gate 2, the model executes <code>read_file</code> and declares the result in a structured header. This is the critical grounding step&mdash;the rule content is now in the model's context window, not just its parametric memory.</p>
    <p><strong>Gate 4: Response.</strong> The model generates its response, informed by the loaded rules. The PRE-FLIGHT header at the top declares which gates passed and which rules were loaded.</p>

    <h3>Discovery Flow</h3>
    <p>The protocol supports two discovery paths to handle different runtime environments. The primary path delegates to a <code>rule-loader</code> skill that returns a structured manifest. The fallback path (Step 2B) has the model grep <code>RULES_INDEX.md</code> directly. Both paths converge at the same point: an ordered list of rule files to load via <code>read_file</code>.</p>

